      "message": "I looked into this and kept `pending`, for two reasons.\n\nFirst, on rebinding: `areContentsTheSame` returns `false` unconditionally, so every surviving row is rebound on every update no matter what `areItemsTheSame` answers. Loosening identity would therefore not save any bind calls; it would only change remove/insert animations into change animations.\n\nSecond, and the reason I would rather keep it: the list handed to the adapter is a concatenation of two independent sources. In CallPresenter.addConferenceParticipant the pending entry is built with `pending \u003d true` and pushed with `Conference.addPending`, and the presenter combines them as `p + pending`. It is removed via `doOnEvent` after a one second delay, while the participant is added to the conference in the subscribe body, so a contact can legitimately appear once from each source for a short window. `pending` is what keeps those two rows distinct, and DiffUtil requires `areItemsTheSame` to be a true identity within a single list.\n\nOn the wording \"mutable participant state\": `ParticipantInfo` exposes `pending` as a `val` on a class whose fields are all read-only, and a transition builds a new instance rather than mutating one. The instability being fixed here is that the *stable ID* changed for a row; identity in DiffUtil has no such immutability requirement across updates.\n\nI have added a comment above the helper to record why those fields are the identity. Happy to drop `pending` if you still prefer it, but I did not want to widen the identity to two concurrent rows without flagging it.",
